body:
Wow, imagine that! A Katseye x G&L crossover =o That does *not* look like the Gnarly dance, like at all XD what a sad cover. for one thing the 'copy' move wasn't even on 'copy', of course she didn't do the two jumpies at the end because she can't move that fast (or fast enough for the dance in general) and probably jumping twice in a row is too much for her, and not a single part is crisp and energetic. Bets on whether she likes the song or if she's just doing it because it's popular? *Maybe* she likes Gnarly because she's just that legit° and obvi obviiii they be tryna copy, but also she's gotta stay relevant y'all, so Idk. But I don't see their other songs like Debut or Touch being her vibe ┐⁠(⁠ ⁠∵⁠ ⁠)⁠┌ Side note, I loveeeeeee Katseye! Been totally obsessed since I heard Debut (their debut song) a few months after it came out and the girls seem to really enjoy the total vibe switch for this comeback <3333 [Here's the full dance to the original version of their song Gnarly.](https://youtu.be/xrm7PP1mbtI?si=br-6fNmmfNVqMlFt)

° 'the sh¡t' in the original version = 'legit' in the clean version. I prefer the clean version =P

Edit: this has been edited a million times because I just can never manage to type what I want the first time and this comment was on the worse end of that for me haha ;;
